1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,985
Hi again. In this video,

2
00:00:02,985 --> 00:00:06,315
we're going to discuss influencing
the people around you.

3
00:00:06,315 --> 00:00:08,250
I'll describe the four steps of

4
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:11,565
influencing and some common
influencing mistakes.

5
00:00:11,565 --> 00:00:13,560
There are a few techniques that

6
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,045
project managers can use to

7
00:00:15,045 --> 00:00:16,665
influence the people
they work with,

8
00:00:16,665 --> 00:00:19,145
both within a team and beyond it.

9
00:00:19,145 --> 00:00:22,879
But first, what do we
mean by influencing?

10
00:00:22,879 --> 00:00:25,385
Influencing is the ability to

11
00:00:25,385 --> 00:00:28,805
alter another person's
thinking or behaviors.

12
00:00:28,805 --> 00:00:31,610
We'll discuss the concept
of influencing in

13
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:35,555
the context of our Plant Pals
project at Office Green.

14
00:00:35,555 --> 00:00:38,330
Let's say that your team
would like to partner with

15
00:00:38,330 --> 00:00:39,950
a well-known chocolate
manufacturer

16
00:00:39,950 --> 00:00:41,740
to create a bundle deal.

17
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:44,900
With this deal, the client
could choose to add on

18
00:00:44,900 --> 00:00:46,355
a high-quality chocolate bar

19
00:00:46,355 --> 00:00:48,550
with each plant they purchase.

20
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,650
You decide to send an initial
email to a partnership

21
00:00:51,650 --> 00:00:53,479
Manager at the
chocolate manufacturer

22
00:00:53,479 --> 00:00:55,369
to gauge their
interest in the idea,

23
00:00:55,369 --> 00:00:58,535
and ultimately influence
